WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.236 --> 00:00:06.059
Jack Gibson hurried out of the car and ran to the swimming pool.

2
00:00:06.079 --> 00:00:07.400
"Awesome!" he thought.

3
00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:29.973
The pool at the apartment complex was large with two lap Best of all, it was only steps

4
00:00:30.073 --> 00:00:32.235
away from his family's new apartment.

5
00:00:33.035 --> 00:00:35.137
He was going to love California!

6
00:00:35.157 --> 00:00:37.779
"Jack!" Luke called out.

7
00:00:38.439 --> 00:00:39.520
Jack didn't turn around.

8
00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:44.523
He loved his four-year-old brother, but the last three days in the car with him had felt like

9
00:00:44.623 --> 00:00:45.504
three years.

10
00:00:46.805 --> 00:00:49.947
He couldn't wait to get to his new bedroom and lock the door.

11
00:00:50.988 --> 00:00:52.909
"Jack!" Luke yelled louder.

12
00:00:53.609 --> 00:00:55.311
Jack turned around and scowled.

13
00:00:55.331 --> 00:01:00.698
"What?" "Mommy and Daddy said to bring stuff to our new apartment."

14
00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:06.043
Jack walked back to the car and took a bag of clothes from the trunk.

15
00:01:09.806 --> 00:01:12.849
Fortunately, his dad had moved the furniture in the week before.

16
00:01:13.930 --> 00:01:16.352
Jack and his family headed to their new apartment.

17
00:01:18.714 --> 00:01:23.918
Inside, Jack saw it was tiny, less than half the size of their house back in Oklahoma.

18
00:01:25.399 --> 00:01:26.616
But that was okay.

19
00:01:26.636 --> 00:01:28.317
Their old house didn't have a pool.

20
00:01:28.337 --> 00:01:30.077
"Where's my bedroom?"

21
00:01:30.397 --> 00:01:31.017
Jack asked.

22
00:01:31.838 --> 00:01:33.698
He saw his parents frown at each other.

23
00:01:33.718 --> 00:01:38.019
"Um we didn't want you to worry," his mother mumbled.

24
00:01:38.039 --> 00:01:39.580
"Worry about what?"

25
00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:40.600
Jack asked.

26
00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:43.741
"You and Luke will be sharing a room."

27
00:01:43.761 --> 00:01:46.442
"Yay!" Luke yelled.

28
00:01:46.462 --> 00:01:49.143
"Ugh," Jack muttered.

29
00:01:49.843 --> 00:01:55.608
Fourteen-year-olds were not supposed to share bedrooms with four-year-olds.

30
00:01:55.628 --> 00:01:58.409
"California's housing prices are much higher than Oklahoma's.

31
00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:03.772
We couldn't afford a bigger place, especially one with a pool," his father said.

32
00:02:04.732 --> 00:02:06.093
Jack walked into the bedroom.

33
00:02:08.514 --> 00:02:13.396
It had just enough room for two twin beds, a small dresser, and a tiny closet.

34
00:02:14.356 --> 00:02:18.858
On the other side of the wall, in the next apartment, a popular song from the Long-Hair Boys

35
00:02:18.898 --> 00:02:21.519
band was playing: "Baby, don't you see.

36
00:02:21.679 --> 00:02:22.700
You're my destiny."

37
00:02:36.804 --> 00:02:38.165
Jack rolled his eyes.

38
00:02:38.825 --> 00:02:42.127
Whoever lived next door had horrible taste in music.

39
00:02:43.148 --> 00:02:48.531
Luke sang along, off-key: "'Listen to my pleas.

40
00:02:49.031 --> 00:02:52.293
You're the one for me.

41
00:02:52.313 --> 00:02:54.854
Ooh, baby, baby, baby.

42
00:02:54.874 --> 00:02:57.776
Ooh, baby, baby, baby.'"

43
00:02:58.604 --> 00:03:00.686
Jack sank down on one of the beds.

44
00:03:02.247 --> 00:03:05.310
The only good thing about this apartment was the swimming pool.

45
00:03:06.991 --> 00:03:09.133
He looked at his parents, who stood in the doorway.

46
00:03:09.153 --> 00:03:10.975
"Can I go to the pool?

47
00:03:11.475 --> 00:03:13.617
I need to be ready for swim team practice tomorrow."

48
00:03:14.678 --> 00:03:17.600
"You need to unpack your things," his mother said.

49
00:03:18.861 --> 00:03:20.663
Jack grinned and held up something.

50
00:03:22.344 --> 00:03:24.826
"Look—I already unpacked a towel and my swimsuit!"

51
00:03:25.607 --> 00:03:26.768
His parents smiled.

52
00:03:27.372 --> 00:03:30.254
"Don't stay at the pool too long," his mom said.

53
00:03:30.794 --> 00:03:31.955
"You have a lot to do."

54
00:03:31.975 --> 00:03:34.756
"Thanks!" Jack exclaimed.

55
00:03:35.336 --> 00:03:38.038
As he rushed toward the pool, a voice rang out.

56
00:03:38.058 --> 00:03:41.380
"Slow down, young man!"

57
00:03:42.460 --> 00:03:43.160
Jack halted.

58
00:03:44.021 --> 00:03:46.142
An older woman sat in a lounge chair.

59
00:03:47.123 --> 00:03:50.424
She was built like a linebacker and wrinkled like a raisin.

60
00:03:50.444 --> 00:03:54.687
"It's rude to stare," she said with a scowl.

61
00:03:54.707 --> 00:04:00.967
"Sorry." Jack threw his towel onto a chair and dived into the pool.

62
00:04:04.350 --> 00:04:06.011
There were only a couple of other swimmers.

63
00:04:06.992 --> 00:04:09.874
Ahh. The water temperature was perfect.

64
00:04:09.894 --> 00:04:12.136
"Don't splash!"

65
00:04:12.496 --> 00:04:13.457
the old woman yelled.

66
00:04:14.038 --> 00:04:15.399
Jack tried to ignore her.

67
00:04:15.959 --> 00:04:18.021
He swam the breaststroke across the pool.

68
00:04:21.624 --> 00:04:26.408
He'd been the best at breaststroke on his team in Oklahoma, and at freestyle too.

69
00:04:27.188 --> 00:04:29.289
He hoped he'd be the best on the team here too.

70
00:04:30.669 --> 00:04:33.750
Now that he had a pool, he could practice more than ever.

71
00:04:33.770 --> 00:04:36.471
"You're raising your head too high.

72
00:04:36.651 --> 00:04:39.352
It's slowing you down," the old woman snapped.

73
00:04:40.512 --> 00:04:42.233
Jack ignored her and kept swimming.

74
00:04:45.334 --> 00:04:47.735
"And cup your hands when they enter the water!"

75
00:04:48.955 --> 00:04:50.836
Jack didn't even glance her way.

76
00:04:55.112 --> 00:04:57.193
Someone started swimming in the other lap lane.

77
00:04:57.733 --> 00:04:58.353
He looked over.

78
00:04:59.094 --> 00:05:01.555
A girl about his age was doing the backstroke.

79
00:05:05.056 --> 00:05:07.157
He swam over to her and flashed a smile.

80
00:05:07.177 --> 00:05:08.838
"Hey, I'm Jack.

81
00:05:09.418 --> 00:05:10.478
I just moved here today."

82
00:05:10.498 --> 00:05:12.899
"Welcome. I'm Laura."

83
00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:14.940
She dog-paddled next to him.

84
00:05:18.422 --> 00:05:23.504
She was very cute, with brown eyes, freckles, and a long, dark ponytail.

85
00:05:24.620 --> 00:05:28.582
"The only thing better than swimming," Jack thought, "is swimming with a cute girl!"

86
00:05:28.602 --> 00:05:30.383
"Do you like living here?"

87
00:05:30.643 --> 00:05:31.064
he asked.

88
00:05:31.084 --> 00:05:32.124
"I do.

89
00:05:32.764 --> 00:05:34.946
The pool is awesome, and our neighbors are nice."

90
00:05:34.966 --> 00:05:39.188
"Hey! Keep the noise down," the old woman said.

91
00:05:39.208 --> 00:05:41.049
"You call that nice?"

92
00:05:41.369 --> 00:05:41.989
Jack muttered.

93
00:05:42.830 --> 00:05:44.551
Laura smiled politely at the woman.

94
00:05:45.111 --> 00:05:46.592
"Hello, I'm Laura Perez."

95
00:05:48.193 --> 00:05:49.673
The woman didn't smile back.

96
00:05:49.693 --> 00:05:51.494
"Ellen Wilson.

97
00:05:51.915 --> 00:05:52.795
Call me Mrs.

98
00:05:52.875 --> 00:05:54.136
Wilson. Or ma'am.

99
00:05:54.844 --> 00:05:56.525
I moved here three days ago."

100
00:05:56.545 --> 00:06:00.406
"Welcome to Sunnyside Apartments, ma'am," Laura said.

101
00:06:00.426 --> 00:06:02.446
"I'm Jack Gibson."

102
00:06:03.026 --> 00:06:06.667
Jack smiled at the old lady, just to show Laura he was a friendly guy.

103
00:06:07.528 --> 00:06:09.148
Mrs. Wilson scowled at him.

104
00:06:09.808 --> 00:06:11.109
"Want to race across the pool?"

105
00:06:11.489 --> 00:06:12.469
Jack asked Laura.

106
00:06:13.189 --> 00:06:13.870
Laura grinned.

107
00:06:13.890 --> 00:06:17.110
"Sure." Jack smiled for real now.

108
00:06:18.291 --> 00:06:20.371
Laura would be amazed by his speed.

109
00:06:20.992 --> 00:06:24.778
He wouldn't swim too fast, just enough to beat her by five meters or so.

110
00:06:25.739 --> 00:06:26.980
He didn't want to humiliate her.

111
00:06:27.581 --> 00:06:31.604
Afterward, he could give pointers on her technique—not in a mean way like Mrs.

112
00:06:31.644 --> 00:06:35.628
Wilson. His way would be helpful, and Laura would appreciate it.

113
00:06:35.648 --> 00:06:39.771
"I'll referee the race," Mrs.

114
00:06:39.831 --> 00:06:40.472
Wilson said.

115
00:06:40.492 --> 00:06:42.794
"Great!" Laura exclaimed.

116
00:06:42.814 --> 00:06:45.316
"Great," Jack muttered.

117
00:06:46.037 --> 00:06:49.280
He and Laura got out of the water and stood at the edge of the pool.

118
00:06:51.824 --> 00:06:57.569
"Young man, I hope you display better form in freestyle than in the breaststroke," Mrs.

119
00:06:57.629 --> 00:06:58.290
Wilson said.

120
00:06:59.271 --> 00:07:01.513
Jack forced himself to smile politely.

121
00:07:02.053 --> 00:07:03.014
"I'll do my best."

122
00:07:03.955 --> 00:07:05.656
"Take your mark," Mrs.

123
00:07:05.696 --> 00:07:06.377
Wilson said.

124
00:07:07.238 --> 00:07:09.500
Jack and Laura got into diving positions.

125
00:07:09.520 --> 00:07:11.501
"Go!" Mrs.

126
00:07:11.541 --> 00:07:12.242
Wilson yelled.

127
00:07:14.204 --> 00:07:18.708
Jack got off to a quick start, entering the water with just a slight splash.

128
00:07:22.316 --> 00:07:26.059
He pushed through the water with forceful strokes and strong scissors kicks.

129
00:07:27.520 --> 00:07:30.523
He reminded himself not to get too far ahead of Laura.

130
00:07:31.163 --> 00:07:32.344
He glanced at her lane.

131
00:07:33.025 --> 00:07:34.626
She was swimming right next to him.

132
00:07:38.970 --> 00:07:41.652
he realized, "she might be a little ahead of me."

133
00:07:41.672 --> 00:07:43.613
"Focus, Jack!"

134
00:07:43.974 --> 00:07:45.215
Mrs. Wilson called out.

135
00:07:46.296 --> 00:07:51.640
Jack missed a breath, which made him lose more focus, and Laura quickly pulled ahead of him.

136
00:07:52.768 --> 00:07:57.709
Jack sped up, suddenly swimming as if he were racing for a spot on the Olympic team.

137
00:08:01.390 --> 00:08:03.931
But Laura touched the wall of the pool first.

138
00:08:05.411 --> 00:08:07.492
"Laura is the winner," Mrs.

139
00:08:07.532 --> 00:08:08.172
Wilson said.

140
00:08:08.192 --> 00:08:11.613
"The clear winner.

141
00:08:12.373 --> 00:08:14.754
That makes Jack the clear loser."

142
00:08:16.054 --> 00:08:17.255
Laura smiled at Jack.

143
00:08:17.275 --> 00:08:18.835
"Good race.

144
00:08:19.415 --> 00:08:19.975
That was fun."

145
00:08:21.596 --> 00:08:23.584
He nodded but didn't smile back.

146
00:08:24.705 --> 00:08:26.225
It was a terrible race!

147
00:08:27.345 --> 00:08:30.186
In Oklahoma he'd never been beaten by a girl.

148
00:08:30.826 --> 00:08:32.767
He'd hardly ever been beaten by anyone.

149
00:08:33.787 --> 00:08:35.888
"Good freestyle form," Mrs.

150
00:08:35.928 --> 00:08:36.588
Wilson said.

151
00:08:36.608 --> 00:08:38.708
"Thanks," Jack replied.

152
00:08:38.728 --> 00:08:41.769
"I was talking to Laura," Mrs.

153
00:08:41.809 --> 00:08:42.429
Wilson said.

154
00:08:42.449 --> 00:08:48.011
"Young man, your breathing was completely off and your legs were a mile apart.

155
00:08:48.451 --> 00:08:52.072
If you're going to be a swimmer, you—" Splash!

156
00:08:54.354 --> 00:08:58.058
Jack dived back into the pool before she was finished speaking.
